  The controller's read: Origin::Personal is assigned only at shelves.rs `origin()`, through `self.personal`, which only Shelves::of sets, and `of` always sets the project shelf. So the arm is unreachable by construction. Verify that yourself.

  The round stopped IMPL-BLOCKED. Its boxed verify failed twice on engine::broker::admission::tests::every_steps_door_rechecks_the_lease_its_attempt_holds (b9's code; see below), which passes on the host alone and in the full lib (1226 of 1226). Its implement visits changed no code after beb59118.
- 9526691e, the controller's: decision 0083's personal-shelf addendum Status moves to "accepted — operator ruled 2026-10-17 on slice A (PR #722) and 2026-10-21 on slice B (#697)", per ruling (d).

No host exact-coverage gate has reported on this branch since the rebase onto 68c41bcd. The one on 78abaa94 ran every shard green and missed only the four gaps 697b5 closes. This landing re-runs coverage.

Every review position, panel member or chief, is READ-ONLY: it changes no tracked file and makes no commit, whatever this text asks below. It reports each finding. Only the implement phase fixes a finding the review returns.

Judge, on HEAD (the base is 68c41bcd):
1. The queued-provenance HIGH is closed end to end. Reproduce on target/debug/brokkr in a scratch folder repository with its own HOME and XDG_CONFIG_HOME:
   - an entry queued on a personal shelf, then admitted under a different XDG_CONFIG_HOME, is refused with QueuedShelfUnplaced's exact text, naming both shelves, and runs nothing;
   - the same entry, admitted under neither XDG_CONFIG_HOME nor HOME, ends with "(it places none)";
   - an entry edited after queueing so its shelf names neither shelf is refused at the rebuilt start, not only at admission;
   - an entry on the workspace's own shelf, or on the personal shelf the process places, still admits and runs.
2. 697b5 changed no behaviour. personal_library's `expect` cannot be reached from any caller, including a resumed run and a queued launch. Each new test fails when what it binds is removed: run one removal control in a scratch edit and restore it. No refusal text, public item or baseline moved in beb59118.
